    "_sources": {
      "ar_school_immunization": {
        "name": "Arkansas School Immunization Exemptions by School District",
        "url": "https://healthy.arkansas.gov/programs-services/community-family-child-health/immunizations/",
        "organization": "Arkansas Department of Health",
        "organization_url": "https://healthy.arkansas.gov/",
        "description": "School vaccination exemptions from the Arkansas Department of Health's Act 676 of 2019 report, a single workbook covering school years 2013-14 through 2024-25. Rows are the 263 public school districts and open-enrollment charters; columns are school years, each giving the district's exemption count, total student count, and exemption percentage. Records here are one per school district per school year, as published - 3,055 in total. All grades are combined; the source reports no per-grade, per-antigen, or per-exemption-type breakdown, and does not cover private or home-schooled students. Cells reading 'N/A' (a district or charter not operating that year) carry neither a count nor an enrollment and are omitted rather than written as zero, which accounts for 101 of the 3,156 district-years. Each record carries the county FIPS taken from the LEA code, whose first two digits are Arkansas's county number in alphabetical order and therefore in county FIPS order; this attributes a district wholly to the county of its administrative office, so a county aggregate covers the districts administered from that county rather than every pupil resident in it, and the few districts that straddle a county line are counted on one side only. The two earliest years are not comparable to the rest: the statewide exemption rate is 0.13% for 2013-14 and 0.16% for 2014-15, then jumps to 1.29% for 2015-16 and rises steadily thereafter, which reflects a change in what the state collected rather than a tenfold change in exemptions.",
